#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Lessons as design rules"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Every rule on this page comes from something that went wrong while this architecture was running with real data. We've written each one in its general form. Many of the [principles]{1} and contract clauses exist because of them. So if a rule looks over-cautious, it's because not following it once cost us something."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Measuring and verifying"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Tuning and measurement harnesses call the real production code path. If a required input is missing, they raise an error; they never quietly fall back to something else."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Calibrate a detector's positive class on independent real-world captures, such as different devices and damaged copies, not on clean re-renders of the same source."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "A processing chain carries assumptions about what it's aimed at. When you re-aim it, re-validate every stage, because downstream you can't tell a signal that was deleted from one that was never there."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "A mitigation isn't done until a measurement on representative data shows that it works."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "\"Deployed\" is a claim about the running process. To check it, ask the live system for a marker that only the new version emits."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Check the thing itself, such as the deployed state or the filled tables, and not a status line or a cached plan."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Just because the schema accepts a configuration doesn't prove it does anything. Read the deployed object back to confirm it, and delete any inert configuration that looks as if it's in charge."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Idempotency, delivery and concurrency"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Remove duplicates at two independent layers. The orchestrator rejects a run identifier it has already seen, and the work itself stops early if it finds a terminal state."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Write to a temporary location and then move the result into place in one atomic step, so a replay never sees half-finished output."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "In upsert guards, a human decision outranks a redelivery. A guard tests the condition that would make the operation wrong, not a status label."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Test every migration on a database it has already been applied to, because \"idempotent\" is a claim about the second run. Never cache facts about the schema indefinitely."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Enforce mutual exclusion in the database, with a unique key, and select and acquire in a single statement. Check the lease before the first write."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Judge health from a heartbeat, not from process statistics. Isolate failures item by item, by quarantining the bad item and carrying on, so one poisoned input can't jam the whole pipeline."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Chain stages by handing work from one to the next, so fallback paths can't be reached. A job's timeout is at least the sum of its tasks' budgets."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "With a transactional table format, every statement is a commit. So batch work into set-based operations, and keep the work at the end of a run to a fixed number of round trips."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Stores and data of record"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Before anything empties a store, find out whether it's the source of record. Archive what succeeded, send rejects to a dead-letter location with a reason, and derive locations from content hashes."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Keep one manifest of what a secondary store holds. Derive the sync and lag checks from it, and test that every reporting source has something writing to it."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Reconcile primary and secondary stores. A job reporting success tells you nothing about a write it made after its own commit."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Never deploy from a tree with uncommitted changes. Alert when data goes stale, not only when a job fails."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Validate references against the authoritative registry with a foreign key. Rather than rewriting bad history, stop new bad records from being added."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Identity, grants and infrastructure as code"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "A declarative permission block is the complete set, so it revokes anything it doesn't list. Before you act on a hypothesis, confirm it with read-only queries against the live system."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "An identity isn't configuration. Recreating a resource can create a new principal, so pass principals in as parameters, and keep code that verifies every layer of grants."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Version privileges alongside the schema, including the default privileges for objects that future migrations will create."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Give a deploy identity exactly the rights it needs to create what it deploys, make it the owner of what it deploys, and copy deployment state rather than trees of files."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Check privileges before the first run under a new identity. A right to manage something without the right to create it can turn into a drop you can't undo."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Declare an explicit dependency between a permission and the first thing that uses it. One successful apply may just have been lucky ordering."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Plan and apply take their state and path parameters from one shared definition. Run the first apply somewhere a failure is cheap."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Scope credentials to the single step that needs them."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Render environment-specific artefacts from the deployment tool's resolved output, and have each service report, on a health endpoint, which environment it believes it's in."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Data protection and provenance"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Before any destructive drop, prove the provenance of each object separately. A schema or a repository isn't a unit of provenance."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Write exclusion rules by kind of data, such as spreadsheets or exported learner lists, not by file names someone remembers."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Normalise external identities once, at the boundary, and enforce the normal form with a constraint."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Failure signalling"
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Make missing data fail loudly, for example with strict undefined values, and pin that strictness with a test."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Keep \"refused bad input\" and \"system broken\" in separate counters and separate statuses."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "A tolerated failure matches, and names, the specific error it tolerates."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Every path that produces a stored derived value calls the same single implementation, and tests exercise the fallback paths."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/lessons.md
msgid "Every recurring job has a quick \"nothing to do\" exit, taking seconds on the cheapest compute. Automation never starts paid compute without consent."
msgstr ""
